From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:17:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 085/119] Loop store promotion: an element a loop reads and
 writes stays in a register

In "av[i] := av[i] + x" inner loops every iteration reloaded the element it
had just stored, which puts a store-to-load forwarding latency on the
loop-carried path. optloop.optimize_loop_stores (-O3, with node DFA) keeps
such an element in a register temp: it is loaded once before the loop
(guarded by the loop condition, and only if the first statement of the body
that is not a local update stores to it), read from the temp, and every
store still goes to memory as well, so other reads see it. Only when the
loop has no calls, exceptions, labels or impure inline nodes, every store
goes to the element itself, a temp or a local whose address is never taken,
and the element's address does not change in the loop.
tests/test/opt/tloopstore1.pp.
